WEBVTT

00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:14,700
Can you recommend ingredients for a cancer patient that is dairy-free?

00:00:15,860 --> 00:00:18,960
Ingredients for what?

00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:30,540
So I'm very familiar with eating dairy-free. We have a lot of people in our family that are dairy-free for other reasons.

00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:34,660
As far as a smoothie goes,

00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:43,540
we never buy milk in our house, so we don't have any cow's milk.

00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:50,180
What do we use to add to a smoothie? Well, personally, for me, for my smoothie, I don't add

00:00:51,060 --> 00:01:02,500
any, quote, unquote, nut milk at all. My wife does. She likes coconut toasted coconut. I can't

00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:10,420
remember the brand. It comes in a plastic bottle. It's toasted coconut, and they have an organic one of

00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:18,420
those now. And that's what we use for a substitute for milk in our house. Like if we had a bowl of

00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:25,620
granola cereal or something, I would use that toasted coconut. I think we're just used to that. To

00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:37,380
be it, we haven't had dairy cows milk in our house for a decade or so or more. So my wife has been

00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:49,940
dairy-free for a long time. So we would add that toasted coconut milk. I'm sorry, I can't tell you the

00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:59,220
brand name of it. Maybe somebody else can remember if they think of that. If they use that same product,

00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:07,780
that rings the bell. But that's what we use as far as adding to a smoothie. Now, other things that

00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:14,980
you could add to a smoothie is coconut yogurt. So there are all the yogurts out there. There's coconut

00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:23,860
yogurts out there. You could use that in a smoothie. That would be something. Forage your brand makes

00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:34,260
and it makes probably the best quality yogurt. It's organic. Forage your brand. If you could get that

00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:45,140
locally, they may have a vanilla and they have a played yogurt brand. I don't think they have

00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:50,580
the berry. You don't have to add your own berries and stuff. But that's probably the best quality yogurt.

00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:58,260
Thank you, Stacey. It is Khalifa Farms coconut milk. That's the one that is an organic coconut milk.

00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:04,660
Toasted coconut milk. They have an organic almond milk. Both of those are good. Khalifa Farms.

00:03:04,660 --> 00:03:10,100
They're getting to be a fairly big brand now. You can get them in most grocery stores now.

00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:21,380
Comes in a plastic bottle. And then forage your brand is they make a sour cream. That's actually

00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:29,300
pretty good. That's dairy free. They make a, and I believe that's organic. And they also make a

00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:40,100
the yogurts that are organic. That's my daughter feeds my granddaughter. My two granddaughters and

00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:49,940
her family just love that yogurt. So that's what they use typically. That Khalifa Farms also has a

00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:57,540
coffee creamer or what it's worth. There's lots of other coffee creamers that are dairy free

00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:09,220
out there too. But I like that brand Khalifa Farms. Can I chat in? Yeah. Can you hear me? Yes.

00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:15,540
Because okay. Do you have any concern at all about all the gums in these non-dairy

00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:25,140
milk and yogurt? Not really. Because you're not eating that much of it.

00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:38,420
And yes, there could be some negatives to different gums. But a lot of them do act kind of like an

00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:46,900
indigestible fiber. So you're not absorbing a lot of them. Now you can have sensitivities to

00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:55,220
different gums. So if you use some of these products and you feel off at all in any way,

00:04:55,220 --> 00:05:00,900
your gut feels off or you have any type of symptoms, brain fog or anything like that.

00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:11,700
You can't have sensitivity. So the Cyrex Array 10 does test for different gums. So if you have

00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:18,420
that thought process that you may have a sensitivity to that, then that's possible. I understand

00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:25,700
everybody's a little bit different. But we buy a jug of that Khalifa Farms toasted coconut. And

00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:30,100
typically we end up throwing part of it away because we just don't go through, you know, it's just

00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:34,740
my wife and I at our house. So then the grandkids come over. They don't really use it that much.

00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:41,700
So we don't really go through it. So it's not like we're consuming a lot of it.

00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:49,700
But yeah, there is a possibility of having a sensitivity to those to anything really.

00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:56,420
Anything you eat a lot of, you could develop a sensitivity too. So you do have to be aware of that.

00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:59,560
Thank you.

